{"name":"Blue Hour","hex":"#0034ab","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue hour","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The period of twilight when the Sun is approximately 4-8° below the horizon and the sky is within a range of blue colors."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_hour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Hour","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Hour is a collaboration album by jazz saxophonist Stanley Turrentine and The Three Sounds recorded in 1961 for the Blue Note label and performed by Turrentine with Gene Harris, Andrew Simpkins and Bill Dowdy. The album was reissued in 2000 with an additional disc of unreleased recordings, as Blue Hour: The Complete Sessions."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b5/Blue_Hour_%281961_Stanley_Turrentine_and_The_Three_Sounds_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Hour","wikidata":"Q4929253"},{"title":"Blue hour","blocks":[{"text":"The blue hour is the period of twilight when the Sun is at a significant depth below the horizon. During this time, the remaining sunlight takes on a mostly blue shade. This shade differs from the colour of the sky on a clear day, which is caused by Rayleigh scattering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/S%C3%A9_Catedral_de_Bragan%C3%A7a_-_Portugal_%283663183339%29.jpg/330px-S%C3%A9_Catedral_de_Bragan%C3%A7a_-_Portugal_%283663183339%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_hour","wikidata":"Q882565"},{"title":"Hour","blocks":[{"text":"An hour is a unit of time historically reckoned as 1⁄24 of a day and defined contemporarily as exactly 3,600 seconds. There are 60 minutes in an hour, and 24 hours in a day."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/AnalogClockAnimation1_2hands_1h_in_6sec.gif/330px-AnalogClockAnimation1_2hands_1h_in_6sec.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hour","wikidata":"Q25235"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Max_Klinger_%281857-1920%29_l%27_Heure_bleue%2C1890%2Chuile_sur_toile_191%2C5_x_176_cm%2C_Mus%C3%A9e_des_Beaux-Arts_de_Leipzig.jpg/120px-Max_Klinger_%281857-1920%29_l%27_Heure_bleue%2C1890%2Chuile_sur_toile_191%2C5_x_176_cm%2C_Mus%C3%A9e_des_Beaux-Arts_de_Leipzig.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Max_Klinger_%281857-1920%29_l%27_Heure_bleue%2C1890%2Chuile_sur_toile_191%2C5_x_176_cm%2C_Mus%C3%A9e_des_Beaux-Arts_de_Leipzig.jpg/250px-Max_Klinger_%281857-1920%29_l%27_Heure_bleue%2C1890%2Chuile_sur_toile_191%2C5_x_176_cm%2C_Mus%C3%A9e_des_Beaux-Arts_de_Leipzig.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Max_Klinger_%281857-1920%29_l%27_Heure_bleue%